{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.BraidPathNotCoordination","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BraidPathNotCoordination","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Finset.Card","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Finset.Image","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BraidPathNotCoordination.not_coordination_regular","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BraidPathNotCoordination.not_coordination_regular","kind":"theorem","line":221,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BraidPathNotCoordination.lean#L221-L225","doc":"Sharper: the braid is not coordination-regular at any `A ≥ 4`, so no choice\nof nucleon rescues the reading. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BraidPathNotCoordination.braid_degree_ne_coordination_degree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BraidPathNotCoordination.braid_degree_ne_coordination_degree","kind":"theorem","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BraidPathNotCoordination.lean#L215-L219","doc":"**The separation.** At `A ≥ 4` no nucleon of the braid attains the\ncoordination degree, so the braid's `A - 1` cannot be the block's `A - 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BraidPathNotCoordination.two_lt_coordination_degree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BraidPathNotCoordination.two_lt_coordination_degree","kind":"theorem","line":209,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BraidPathNotCoordination.lean#L209-L213","doc":"At `A ≥ 4` the coordination degree the block asks of every nucleon exceeds\n`2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BraidPathNotCoordination.degree_le_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BraidPathNotCoordination.degree_le_two","kind":"theorem","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BraidPathNotCoordination.lean#L203-L207","doc":"**The braid's per-nucleon degree never exceeds 2** — derived from the\nmeasured bond set, not posited as a closed form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BraidPathNotCoordination.incident_subset","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BraidPathNotCoordination.incident_subset","kind":"theorem","line":190,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BraidPathNotCoordination.lean#L190-L201","doc":"Every braid bond incident to nucleon `k` is `(k-1, k)` or `(k, k+1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BraidPathNotCoordination.degree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BraidPathNotCoordination.degree","kind":"def","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BraidPathNotCoordination.lean#L186-L188","doc":"Per-nucleon degree in the braid's bond set: the bonds incident to `k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BraidPathNotCoordination.card_bonds_eq_choose_two_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BraidPathNotCoordination.card_bonds_eq_choose_two_iff","kind":"theorem","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BraidPathNotCoordination.lean#L173-L182","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BraidPathNotCoordination.sub_one_lt_choose_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BraidPathNotCoordination.sub_one_lt_choose_two","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BraidPathNotCoordination.lean#L153-L171","doc":"**`P_A = K_A` only for `A ≤ 2`.** The braid's bond count equals the complete\ngraph's bond count `C(A,2)` exactly when `A ≤ 2` — the deuteron is the only\nnucleus whose braid bond set is the fully coordinated cluster. At `A = 3`, where\nthe block calibrates, the counts already differ (`2` against `3`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BraidPathNotCoordination.handshake_forces_le_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BraidPathNotCoordination.handshake_forces_le_two","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BraidPathNotCoordination.lean#L128-L151","doc":"**A cluster cannot carry the braid's bond count and the block's degree at\nonce above `A = 2`.**\n\nThe hypothesis `handshake` is the identity `∑_v deg v = 2·|E|` specialised to a\n`z`-regular cluster (`QOU.Mass.CoordinationBinding.coordination_handshake`\nproves it for `K_A`). Feeding it the braid's measured `|E| = A - 1` together\nwith the block's `z = A - 1` forces `A ≤ 2`.\n\nStated with `edges` and `z` as arguments so the two inputs are visible and\nneither is baked in. A hypothesis `1 ≤ A` was carried in a first draft and the\nlinter showed it unused — the bound holds for every `A`, so it is dropped rather\nthan kept for decoration. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BraidPathNotCoordination.braid_count_eq_coordination_degree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BraidPathNotCoordination.braid_count_eq_coordination_degree","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BraidPathNotCoordination.lean#L118-L124","doc":"**The coincidence.** The braid's *edge count* and the block's *vertex\ndegree* are the same function of `A`, so no value of `A` can tell them apart.\nThis is the statement a table of matching rows establishes, and it is weaker\nthan it looks — it is an identity of two arithmetic expressions, not evidence\nthat the two counts are the same object. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BraidPathNotCoordination.card_bonds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BraidPathNotCoordination.card_bonds","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BraidPathNotCoordination.lean#L113-L116","doc":"**The braid's bond count is `A - 1`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BraidPathNotCoordination.succPair_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BraidPathNotCoordination.succPair_injective","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BraidPathNotCoordination.lean#L108-L111","doc":"`k ↦ (k, k+1)` is injective — its first component already is. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BraidPathNotCoordination.coordinationDegree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BraidPathNotCoordination.coordinationDegree","kind":"def","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BraidPathNotCoordination.lean#L103-L106","doc":"The block's per-nucleon coordination number `z(A) = A - 1`: the degree of a\nvertex in the fully coordinated cluster `K_A`. Mirrors\n`QOU.Mass.CoordinationBinding.coordination_degree`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BraidPathNotCoordination.bonds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BraidPathNotCoordination.bonds","kind":"def","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BraidPathNotCoordination.lean#L97-L101","doc":"The braid's inter-nucleon bond set, as measured on `atom_braid_word_3A`:\ngenerator `3k+2` joins nucleon `k` to nucleon `k+1`, for `k < A - 1`. This is\nthe path graph `P_A`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}